      "content": "But what about the humanitarian side of it though? Like, when sanctions hit the regular people in those countries—causing shortages of food or medicine—doesn't that kind of undermine the moral argument for using them? It feels like the 'accountability' part is just a justification for causing widespread suffering among civilians who didn't even make the policies.",
